# Review: BoardPlugin

The board works as the spec describes at the component level: `BoardArticle` resolves `board.items`
refs reactively (dropping unresolved ones), adds a new Markdown document at a backdrop position, adds
an existing object through a sorted `ObjectPicker` that excludes the board, removes the ref and the
layout cell without deleting the object, and writes moves back with `Obj.update`. But almost none of it
is tested: the only plugin test checks module activation, and the single story renders a default
board with no interactions. The four `op` blocks have no runtime counterparts — `createBoard` is a
`CreateObjectEntry` that does not pass `hidden: true`, and add / remove / move are inline component
callbacks. Attention gates only the toolbar buttons; backdrop add and drag stay live without
attention, against F-6.1. No acceptance scenario or QA test has automation.

Of 31 items: 3 done, 16 untested, 1 partial, 4 diverged, 7 missing.

